From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homescoop <homescoop@ai-ecoverse.invalid>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:35:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wasi: run processes through wasix-command

std::process cannot spawn on wasip1 and tokio has no process module on
WASI. Every spawn site imports Command, Child, Stdio and ExitStatus from
wasix-command instead, which is std's and tokio's on other targets, so
native builds are unchanged. On WASI:
- run_to_completion waits without forwarding signals;
- the interpreter query runs python with -s -P rather than -I: -I implies
  -E, and wasix-python finds its standard library through PYTHONHOME,
  which the kernel sets for the command;
- canonicalize_executable keeps the path (no realpath);
- uv run does not copy entrypoints into an ephemeral environment.
